---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Header from "../../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";
import HairPhaseIllustration from "../../components/HairPhaseIllustration.astro";
import { growthPhases } from "../../data/brand";

const structuredData = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Article",
  headline: "Why consistency matters with home IPL",
  datePublished: "2026-09-14",
  dateModified: "2026-09-14",
  inLanguage: "en-GB",
  author: { "@type": "Organization", name: "CYPH/1" },
  publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "CYPH/1" }
};
---
<BaseLayout title="Why consistency matters with home IPL | CYPH/1" description="Learn why light-based hair reduction is approached as a repeated routine across the natural hair-growth cycle." structuredData={structuredData}>
<Header />
<main id="main" class="article-page"><article>
<header class="article-hero section"><div class="container article-reading">
<p class="eyebrow">Know the cycle · IPL education</p>
<h1 data-reveal>Why consistency matters with home IPL</h1>
<p class="lede">IPL is not a one-off interaction with every hair at once. Hair follicles can be at different points in their natural cycle, which is why light-based hair reduction is approached as a repeated routine over time.</p>
<p class="article-meta">Published 14 September 2026 · General educational content</p>
</div></header>

<section class="section article-section"><div class="container article-reading article-copy">
<p class="section-index">01 / The misconception</p>
<h2 data-reveal>One treatment cannot meet every hair at the same moment.</h2>
<p>Individual follicles do not all move through the hair-growth cycle together. At a given time, some hairs can be actively growing while others are transitioning, resting or shedding.</p>
<p>That asynchronous cycle is important context for understanding why light-based hair reduction is repeated rather than treated as a single event.</p>
</div>
<ol class="container article-phase-grid" aria-label="Four asynchronously cycling hair-growth phases">
{growthPhases.map((phase) => (<li class:list={{ active: phase.active }} data-phase-card><div class="phase-card-meta"><span>{phase.number}</span>{phase.active && <small>Active growth</small>}</div><HairPhaseIllustration phase={phase.name} /><h3>{phase.name}</h3><p class="phase-label">{phase.label}</p></li>))}
</ol></section>

<section class="section article-section"><div class="container article-reading article-copy">
<p class="section-index">02 / Active growth</p><h2 data-reveal>Why anagen matters.</h2>
<p>Anagen is the active-growth phase, when the follicle is producing the hair shaft. General evidence about light-based hair reduction associates treatment with active growth.</p>
<aside class="science-note"><p><strong>The important distinction.</strong> This is general IPL education. It is not a performance claim about a future CYPH/1 device.</p></aside>
</div></section>

<section class="section article-section"><div class="container article-reading article-copy">
<p class="section-index">03 / Repetition</p><h2 data-reveal>The routine follows the cycle.</h2>
<p>Because different hairs can be at different points in the cycle, treatment is repeated over time. This allows treatment occasions to coincide with different hairs as they enter active growth.</p>
<div class="routine-line" data-routine aria-hidden="true"><span>01</span><i></i><span>02</span><i></i><span>03</span><i></i><span>04</span></div>
<p>Consistency therefore describes the principle of returning to a routine across the natural cycle. It does not mean treating continuously, and it does not establish a universal treatment interval.</p>
</div></section>

<section class="section article-section"><div class="container article-reading article-copy">
<p class="section-index">04 / What IPL does not do</p><h2 data-reveal>IPL does not read an individual hair’s phase.</h2>
<p>An IPL device does not identify whether an individual hair is in anagen, catagen, telogen or exogen. Repeated treatment is used because hairs cycle asynchronously—not because the device detects and selects hairs by phase.</p>
<aside class="science-note"><p><strong>“Target the growth”</strong> describes the CYPH/1 treatment principle and our educational focus on the cycle. It is not a claim of phase-detection technology.</p></aside>
</div></section>

<section class="section article-section"><div class="container article-reading article-copy">
<p class="section-index">05 / CYPH/1</p><h2 data-reveal>Why we are not publishing a treatment schedule yet.</h2>
<p>CYPH/1 is still in pre-launch product development. We will not publish an exact treatment frequency, session count or outcome before the final product and its instructions have been selected and verified.</p>
<p>When the CYPH/1 product is ready, its verified instructions—not a generic online schedule—will define how it should be used.</p>
</div></section>

<section class="section article-section" aria-labelledby="sources"><div class="container article-reading article-copy">
<p class="section-index">06 / Sources</p><h2 id="sources" data-reveal>Evidence behind this article.</h2>
<p>This article provides general education about hair growth and IPL. It does not state a treatment frequency, outcome or future-product performance.</p>
<ul class="article-sources">
<li><a href="https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK470321/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NCBI Bookshelf — Anatomy, Hair Follicle</a></li>
<li><a href="https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9917549/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">International Journal of Molecular Sciences — Hair Growth Cycle and Hair Loss</a></li>
<li><a href="https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5475414/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Journal of Cutaneous and Aesthetic Surgery — Photoepilation and Skin Photorejuvenation</a></li>
<li><a href="https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4745852/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Clinical, Cosmetic and Investigational Dermatology — Lasers and Intense Pulsed Light Technology</a></li>
</ul>
<p class="related-link"><a href="/learn/hair-growth-cycle/">Start with the four stages of the hair-growth cycle <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></p>
</div></section>

<section class="section article-cta"><div class="container article-reading"><p class="eyebrow">Cycle. Phase. One.</p><h2 data-reveal>Follow the CYPH/1 journey.</h2><p>Join early access for product-development updates and launch information. Registration is not an order or pre-order.</p><a class="button" href="/">Explore CYPH/1</a></div></section>
</article></main><Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<script>
const reduceMotion=window.matchMedia("(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)").matches;
const targets=document.querySelectorAll("[data-reveal], [data-phase-card], [data-routine]");
if(reduceMotion||!("IntersectionObserver" in window)){targets.forEach(t=>t.classList.add("is-visible"));}else{const observer=new IntersectionObserver(entries=>{entries.forEach(entry=>{if(!entry.isIntersecting)return;entry.target.classList.add("is-visible");observer.unobserve(entry.target);});},{threshold:.18,rootMargin:"0px 0px -8% 0px"});targets.forEach(t=>observer.observe(t));}
</script>

<style>
